\begin{frame}{2. Baseline vs Zero-Trust: The Numbers}
  \framesubtitle{Two live Mininet runs, 2026-09-05: same topology, same 40 devices, same six attacks, same schedule}
  \centering\footnotesize
  \begin{tabular}{@{}lrr@{}}
    \toprule
    \textbf{Metric} & \textbf{Baseline} & \textbf{Zero-trust}\\
    \midrule
    Packet delivery ratio                 & 94.29\,\%      & \textbf{99.10\,\%}\\
    Mean per-device availability (honest) & 85.67\,\%      & \textbf{99.00\,\%}\\
    Honest devices served below 50\,\%    & 5              & \textbf{0}\\
    Tasks lost to timeout                 & 380            & \textbf{58}\\
    p95 task latency                      & 260.0\,ms      & \textbf{134.3\,ms}\\
    Mean task latency                     & \textbf{83.7\,ms} & 88.5\,ms\\
    Throughput                            & 20.74 task/s   & 20.66 task/s\\
    Jain fairness, honest servers only    & 0.689          & \textbf{0.992}\\
    Requests routed to attacker nodes     & 30.5\,\%       & \textbf{12.5\,\%}\\
    Anomalies raised / acted on           & 502 / 0        & 372 / \textbf{33}\\
    Identity spoof (iot38 $\to$ iot1)     & \textbf{ADMITTED} at 19.6\,s & \textbf{REFUSED}\\
    Wrong-key devices admitted            & 2              & \textbf{0}\\
    Trust blocks committed                & none (no ledger)& 649\\
    \midrule
    \multicolumn{3}{@{}l@{}}{\textbf{Containment, onset $\to$ isolation:} sybil 8.2\,s $\cdot$ blackhole 8.7\,s $\cdot$ on-off 9.9\,s $\cdot$ grayhole 11.3\,s}\\
    \multicolumn{3}{@{}l@{}}{\emph{The baseline never contains any of them, because it has no isolation path.}}\\
    \bottomrule
  \end{tabular}

  \vspace{4pt}\scriptsize
  Mean latency is 4.8\,ms \emph{worse} in our arm. The trade is a small cost in
  the mean in exchange for removing the long tail: p95 halves, timeouts fall
  85\,\% and throughput is unchanged.
\end{frame}

