\begin{frame}{3. Engineering Decisions Defended, and What Is Not Done}
  \framesubtitle{Rubric: Software Architecture, Implementation, Integration \& Tech Stack (5 Marks)}
  \scriptsize
  \textbf{Decisions we would defend under questioning}
  \begin{enumerate}\itemsep2pt
    \item \textbf{Power-of-two-choices over argmax.} Argmax is winner-take-all: every request goes to one node until its load catches up. We measured it starving the fleet as $N$ grows, while p2c scales linearly.
    \item \textbf{The flood tell is keyed on the requesting client, never the edge node it lands on.} A server drowning under a flood is telling the truth about being overwhelmed.
    \item \textbf{A detector with no recent evidence abstains} rather than re-asserting a stale verdict. Without this, quarantine became an absorbing state that starved the evidence needed to leave it.
    \item \textbf{Anomaly $A$ is a separate gate, not a fourth term.} A node that lies about its load but serves tasks well holds $T\approx0.44$ and never crosses the isolation line.
    \item \textbf{No literal replay attack was built.} \texttt{verify\_response} pops the nonce on first use, so replay was already impossible; the real gap was fleet-wide key sharing.
  \end{enumerate}

  \vspace{2pt}
  \textbf{Open limitations}
  \begin{itemize}\itemsep1pt
    \item \textbf{RAFT is built, proven and demonstrated, but not wired into the controller.} All 649 blocks of the live run carry \texttt{raft\_term = 0}. Three blockers remain: nobody drives the tick; \texttt{commit()} would block an OpenFlow handler thread for up to 2\,s; a \texttt{None} return is currently discarded silently.
    \item \textbf{DDoS is detection-only}; throttling needs a per-client-IP OpenFlow path. We deferred it rather than shipping half of it.
    \item One run per configuration (no confidence intervals) $\cdot$ detection latency is an upper bound, bounded by the 1\,s poll $\cdot$ scalability past 8 nodes is a queueing simulation $\cdot$ localhost, not multi-host.
  \end{itemize}
\end{frame}

